  "problem": "Suppose $|\\,p\\,|=2$ and the angle between vectors $p$ and $q$ is $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
